          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef partialling_out_dml_ridge(X, T, Y, lam: float = 15.0, n_folds: int = 5) -> tuple[float, float, float]:\n    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=float)\n    T = np.asarray(T, dtype=float)\n    Y = np.asarray(Y, dtype=float)\n    n, p = X.shape\n    I = np.eye(p)\n    y_res, t_res = np.empty(n), np.empty(n)\n    folds = np.array_split(np.arange(n), n_folds)\n    for k in range(n_folds):\n        va = folds[k]\n        tr = np.concatenate([folds[j] for j in range(n_folds) if j != k])\n        A = X[tr].T @ X[tr] + lam * I\n        y_res[va] = Y[va] - X[va] @ np.linalg.solve(A, X[tr].T @ Y[tr])\n        t_res[va] = T[va] - X[va] @ np.linalg.solve(A, X[tr].T @ T[tr])\n    denom = float(np.sum(t_res ** 2))\n    theta_hat = float(np.sum(t_res * y_res) / denom)\n    se_hat = float(np.sqrt(np.sum((t_res * (y_res - theta_hat * t_res)) ** 2)) / denom)\n    return (round(theta_hat, 4), round(se_hat, 4), round(2.0 * 1.96 * se_hat, 4))\n```"
